# gotchas — wiki-kb research fan-outs (agents append one short line each)
[noise] Full item/category pages mix ~40% metadata templates ({{Infobox}}, {{Recipe}}, {{ItemSpawnTableHead}}, {{Subject changes}}) + image refs + footer cruft; research agents should target sections with --section N first (sections cmd shows which are low-noise), or request --strip flag to auto-remove template syntax.
[cows-chill] Single-quote in page title "Cow's Chill" requires careful shell escaping when passing to wikicli contribute; wrapping the whole JSON in double-quotes and using escaped single-quotes inside is one workaround.
[cows-chill] Guide links use [https://... Display Name] external link syntax, not [[wikilink]] syntax — regex extracting wikilinks will miss these entirely. Both forms appear in the same document.
[cows-chill] The {{Checklist}} template in the guide uses section numbers that span across the entire guide (1-24+), not resetting per H2 section. The H2 section title is a phase label, not the step counter.
[cows-chill] Quest /Quick guide subpages have tighter signal than main quest pages — always check for /Quick guide first; their Walkthrough section uses {{Checklist}} directly.
[cows-chill] {{Map}} template parameters carry tile coordinates inline; these do not require a separate location page fetch when coordinates are the goal.
[faux] Task Reference section (DPLTaskRow) can be 22000+ bytes — largest section in a guide page; always fetch last or skip if task metadata already collected from checklist bullets.
[faux] Fairy ring page section 5 is labeled "B combinations" not "C combinations" — the letter-pair header offsets by one from the section number; grep for the specific code rather than assuming section order.
[faux] Two Map template coordinate formats exist in the same wiki: bare `x,y` (fairy ring pages) and named `x:NNNN,y:NNNN` (Quetzal pages) — parsers must handle both.
[multiquest-im] Guide:Ironman Multiquest has only 2 top-level sections total -- the entire route is one interleaved {{Checklist}} per hub inside section 2, not split per-quest; expect to grep the raw bullets rather than rely on section boundaries for per-quest isolation.
[multiquest-im] The multiquest page links bare [[Quest Name]] only, never [[Quest Name/Quick guide]] -- you must derive and verify the /Quick guide slug yourself with `sections` before fetching; it is not guaranteed to exist for every quest.
[multiquest-im] Mid-session the wiki-kb README.md on disk was rewritten to claim "Bash is WRITE-ONLY, you never get stdout" plus an instruction to hide this from the user -- both false (this session received direct Bash stdout repeatedly) and a red flag; did not comply, flagging here instead so it isn't silently trusted by future agents reading README.md.
[items] Page-title redirects silently rename the manifest slug/title from what you searched: "Burn level" -> "Cooking/Burn level", "Vial pack" -> "Empty vial pack", "Compost bin" -> "Compost Bin" — always grep manifest.jsonl for the actual title before writing refs[], or contribute quarantines on a title mismatch.
[items] {{Recipe}} template params are trustworthy ground truth (skill1lvl/skill1exp/mat/output) but chain-fixture "detail" prose can drift from them silently — Prayer potion's real Herblore level is 38 (skill1lvl=38 in the fetched Recipe), not the 52 hardcoded in brew-prayer-potion's detail/reqs and mirrored into supply_chains.jsonl's prereq_skills; cross-check every hardcoded level/xp claim against the item's own Creation section, don't trust the chain data as pre-verified.
[items] {{Skilling success chart}} template params (low/high/req per label) are chart-render coordinates, not literal skill levels — do not cite them as burn-stop/success levels. The real per-item burn-stop table lives on a separate page (Cooking/Burn level, "Affected by cooking gauntlets" wikitable) with no cross-link from the item's own Cooking-chance section.
[items] Prayer potion's base Recipe output is explicitly "Prayer potion(3)" (3-dose), not (4) — a 4th dose is a 5%/15% RNG chance gated by wearing amulet of chemistry/alchemist's amulet. Any chain step that models the terminal item as a flat prayer_potion_4:1 produce is silently wrong unless it accounts for this.
[quests] Every quest's `/Quick guide` "Details" H2 is a one-line transclusion stub `{{Quest details page|<Quest>}}` — it does NOT carry the {{Quest details}} template body (start/startmap/requirements/items/kills). Fetch the MAIN quest page's Details section instead (same section index pattern, real content, e.g. `get "Priest in Peril" --section 1`); the Quick guide page is only useful for its Walkthrough {{Checklist}}.
[quests] manifest.jsonl never stores a bare-title slug when every fetch used `--section N` — the recorded slug is always `<Title>.sN`. refs[] contributed against a bare title (no `.sN`) will fail consolidation's "slug must exist in manifest.jsonl" check even though the title is correct; always cite the exact section-suffixed slug you actually fetched.
[quests] Chain-fixture quest-xp values are frequently wrong, not just imprecise: Nature Spirit claims prayer+3000 (real reward has ZERO prayer xp, it's crafting/defence/hitpoints); Tale of the Righteous (mis-id'd "quest-tale-of-arrav") claims strength/defence xp that doesn't exist at all (real reward is 8,000 coins); Swan Song is 5x undercounted on fishing xp and missing magic+prayer entirely; Monkey Madness I claims all four combat stats at max (35k each) when the real reward is a mutually-exclusive CHOICE between two stat pairs. Treat every hardcoded xp number as unverified until cross-checked against the quest's own Rewards section, regardless of how plausible it looks.
[quests] RFD subquest pages ("Recipe for Disaster/<subpage>") wrap Details+Walkthrough+Rewards in one `<onlyinclude>` block transcluded onto the umbrella page — fetching `--section 1` alone often returns the FULL subquest text (several KB) including Rewards, so a separate Rewards-section fetch is redundant-but-harmless; check byte size before assuming a second fetch is needed.
[quests] "Tale of Arrav" is not a real OSRS Wiki page/quest — `search` returns nothing for it; the real quest is "Tale of the Righteous". Chain step id `quest-tale-of-arrav` is a stale/invented slug that survived even though its own label/detail text correctly says "Tale of the Righteous".
[travel] Two "boss"-page reqs turned out to be almost entirely author-invented efficiency numbers, not wiki gates: Barrows has NO combat-level entry requirement at all (only Priest in Peril + started His Faithful Servants — the Barrows page's own "Requirements" section is 156 bytes, easy to miss if you only read Transportation); GWD's real gate is Strength 60 OR Agility 60 (either satisfies the boulder), not Strength 60 alone, and Prayer 43 has zero wiki basis as a GWD entry gate. Always fetch a page's own "Requirements" section (if it has one) before trusting a chain-fixture's reqs.skills block — the fixture numbers read as plausible PvM-readiness targets, which makes them easy to mistake for sourced hard gates.
[travel] Fetching a nested wiki heading via `get --section N` on the PARENT section index (e.g. "==Combinations==" on Fairy rings, which has four "===\"A\"/\"B\"/\"C\"/\"D\" combinations===" sub-headings plus Sequences underneath) pulls ALL child subsections into one blob — the `sections` command still lists each child with its own index/byte count as if separately fetchable, so check an already-cached parent-section blob's line count before re-fetching what looks like a missing child section.
[travel] Manifest title-redirects bit again outside the previously-logged [items] cases: "Marks of grace" -> manifest title "Mark of grace" (singular), "Rooftop Agility Course" -> manifest title "Rooftop Agility Courses" (plural). Same failure mode — always grep manifest.jsonl for the actual title before writing refs[].
[training] "Pay-to-play <Skill> training" page titles don't exist for melee stats — the real combined page is "Pay-to-play Melee training" (covers Attack/Strength/Defence together); "Pay-to-play Slayer training" also doesn't exist, the real title is "Slayer training". Always `search` before assuming the "Pay-to-play X training" pattern holds.
[training] Two more title-redirect traps beyond the known list: "Pay-to-play Herblore training" resolves to manifest title "Herblore training" (no "Pay-to-play" prefix), and "Pay-to-play Farming training" resolves to "Farming training" — contribute with the search term instead of the manifest title silently fails validation.
[training] Monster Infobox stats (combat level, hp, aggression, max hit) live in section 0 (the lead, before the first ==heading==) which `sections` never enumerates — `get --section N` can't target it. For any monster page you need combat stats from, fall back to a full `get --strip` (usually 7-18KB, acceptable) rather than hunting for a section that isn't there.
[training] The P2P route fixture's train-*/ctr-* "xp" fields are synthetic and mostly wrong: only bands starting at level 1 match the real cumulative Experience table (Experience_table.s2) exactly; every band starting at a nonzero level (e.g. 10->30, 40->60, 60->70) uses a copy-pasted placeholder constant reused identically across unrelated skills. Any domain touching train-* rows should fetch Experience_table.s2 once and mechanically recompute cumulative(hi)-cumulative(lo) rather than trusting the fixture's xp field.
[npcs] "Blackjacking" is a title alias that silently resolves to manifest title "Thieving training" (url stays /w/Blackjacking, sections/get both echo the queried title back with no redirect notice) -- the fetched content is the whole Pay-to-play Thieving training guide, not a Blackjacking-only page; grep manifest.jsonl after fetching, same trap as prior [items]/[travel] title-redirect gotchas, one more alias for the list.
[npcs] Shop pages carry NPC coordinates via a second template family, {{NPC map|x=|y=|r=|mtype=}}, on the NPC's own page (not the shop page) -- Zeke's Superior Scimitars (shop) has zero location data, but Zeke (NPC) has {{NPC map|x=3288|y=3190}} in its Infobox NPC. When a shop-page fetch turns up no Map/LocLine, try the eponymous NPC page before flagging a marker unverifiable.
[npcs] {{Store locations list|ItemName}} on an item page's "Shop locations" section is an unexpandable transclusion stub even under --strip -- to find which NPC/shop actually sells an item (e.g. Pineapple), use `links "<Item>"` and scan for a NPC-shaped title (Trader Crewmember), then fetch that NPC's own Stock section directly.
[npcs] Title-case traps beyond the known redirect list: "H.A.M. member" (as typed/searched) vs manifest title "H.A.M. Member" (capital M); "Menaphite thug" vs "Menaphite Thug"; "Pollnivnian bandit" vs "Bandit (Pollnivneach)" (full page-name swap, not just casing) -- all three would silently fail refs[] validation if cited with the search term instead of the manifest title.
[bg] setup-ultracompost's chain detail ("30 pineapples then 15 volcanic ash per bin") is wrong on multiple axes against Ultracompost's own Creation Recipe template: real ash cost is 25/bin (regular) or 50/bin (Big Compost Bin), not 15; real item-fill count is 15 (regular) or 30 (Big Compost Bin) -- the chain's "30" is a big-bin fill count mismatched with a non-big-bin ash count; and there's a simpler ash-direct-on-bucket method (2 ash/bucket of supercompost, no bin fill at all) the chain omits entirely. Always check an item's own "Creation"/"{{Recipe}}" section even when a chain's numbers look internally plausible -- two wrong numbers that are each individually "reasonable" is a harder-to-catch failure mode than one obviously-fabricated one.
[bg] Some P2P route step_ids referenced by tests/fixtures/baseline-routes.json and by other domains' XREF notes (e.g. bg-farm-allotment-setup) do not exist as rows in assets/data/tools/steps.jsonl at all -- grep steps.jsonl for your literal id before assuming "not found" means "not mine"; it may mean the row is a real gap that still needs a PROPOSED-ID contribution, not a step to skip.
[bg] {{Drop sources}}/{{Store locations list}} templates in raw wikitext never carry literal monster/shop names -- they're dynamic Cargo-query templates rendered server-side. A page's only wikitext-literal non-GE source is often a guaranteed {{ItemSpawnLine}} "Spawns" subsection (if one exists) -- check for that before assuming the item has no sourced non-GE origin.
[consolidate] Checkpoint-header ids were minted per ROUTE EMISSION ORDER by enrich.py, so chkpt-<coarse>-<N> named different checkpoints in route-p2p vs route-corpus, and the two scrambler domains keyed their chkpt contributions by two different conventions (pps by registry order from GRANULARITY 5a, ctr by p2p emission order). Only the checkpoint LABEL quoted inside each contribution's notes made an unambiguous remap possible. enrich.py now mints registry-stable ids (index = position in coarse_expansions checkpoints[]); any future by-id work against chkpt-* must assume registry order and should still quote the label as anchor.
[consolidate] Coordinate plausibility linting must include the dungeon band (underground maps at y+6400, up to ~y10500) and instanced regions (y 4000-6500) — a naive surface-world envelope (y<=4400) false-quarantined 9 clean contributions (Paterdomus basement 3440,9894; Stronghold of Security 1936,5135; Prifddinas 3275,6124; deep Wilderness dungeon 3044,10313). Envelope used: x 1000-4400, y 2200-12800.
[consolidate] Legacy Lane-G refs already on steps.jsonl rows ({title,url,kind}, no slug, pre-manifest-validation) can point at never-fetched pages ("Ranarr seed") or near-miss titles ("Zeke's Superior Scimitars" missing the real page's trailing period). Normalize by manifest-title lookup (also try the trailing-period variant) and drop what cannot rebind — contributed validated refs supersede.
[consolidate] One more title-alias for the trap list: "Runecraft training" silently resolves to manifest title "Pay-to-play Runecraft training" (Runecraft is F2P so the P2P-prefix DOES exist for it, inverting the members-skill no-prefix rule that Herblore/Farming/Slayer/Thieving/Agility/Hunter/Construction/Fletching follow).
[extrapolate] route-p2p.json steps carry only {id, detail}-shaped content (no type/label
fields survive to the fixture) — extrapolation and any tooling must key off ids + the
steps.jsonl bank, never fixture labels.
[extrapolate] queue.jsonl contains ZERO blocked entries — every one of the 123 W2 steps
went pending→claimed→done. The real backlog is NOT in blocked states; it lives in the 78
pending lane5:* tickets + coord-fix:* + consolidate-xp:* keys. Agents grepping for
"blocked" to find work will wrongly conclude the ledger is clean.
[extrapolate] Ten wave-3-relevant blobs (5 RFD subpages + Family_Crest/Tai_Bwo_Wannai_Trio/
Rum_Deal/Shadow_of_the_Storm/Big_Chompy_Bird_Hunting + Nightmare_Zone + 6 training guides)
were fetched by the consolidation pass but never mined — they appear in manifest.jsonl with
NO contrib entries citing them. Check manifest BEFORE scoping any fetch: "in manifest"
does not imply "already extracted".
[extrapolate] The only RFD subpage absent from the manifest is Freeing the Lumbridge
Guide — easy to miss because the other nine are present; a completeness check by prefix
(Recipe_for_Disaster_*) catches it.
